# Astra instruction alignment — 2026-09-08

## Scope and evidence

- Baseline and candidate HEAD: `59b567bc0`; candidate is the six uncommitted instruction files listed below, not the entire dirty checkout.
- Environment: Windows PowerShell, repository-local Markdown review; no engine, editor, implementation, commit, or push operations.
- Baseline: byte-identical originals under `codex/snapshots/20260908-astra-instruction-alignment/`, confirmed by SHA-256 before handoff.
- Reference: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model#instruction-following (fetched in this conversation). Official guidance motivates explicit scope and avoiding conflicting skill instructions; repository safety and verification policies remain authoritative locally.

## Changes

- `AGENTS.md`: dependency-audit trigger aligned with the safety matrix; finished-content independence and C++ approval remain intact.
- `codex/AGENTS.md`: concise objective for short read-only tasks; mutation target and purpose remain required.
- `codex/skills/mcp-release-gate/SKILL.md` and its `references/ops-references.md`: route verification, Git synchronization, authorship, and authorization to canonical policies; preserve full promotion and affected build/live requirements. Unrelated dirty work is preserved rather than requiring a globally clean checkout.
- `codex/skills/unreal-mcp-safety-review/SKILL.md` and its `references/ops-references.md`: independently trigger asset and map workflows; safety-matrix routing remains mandatory for matching risks.

## Static scenario review

These are same-agent decision walkthroughs, not executed end-to-end agent benchmarks or live operations.

| Representative request | Candidate routing and expected boundary |
| --- | --- |
| Find an official documentation page | Brief objective; no asset audit, build, or live smoke solely for reading. |
| Edit prose only | Tier 0; no full Python run or editor smoke solely because the editor is open. |
| Push the authorized documentation change while unrelated work is dirty | Scoped staging and canonical synchronization; preserve unrelated work; stop/reconcile an actual overlap. No automatic main-branch authorization. |
| Modify a material without opening or switching a map | Asset workflow and dependency checks; map workflow only if a map/preview/dirty-package transition arises. |
| Author an asset and create a preview map | Both workflows apply; native map preflight and dirty blockers remain. |
| Promote Python implementation | Frozen candidate plus complete passing full evidence and affected checks; focused passes cannot replace full. |
| Modify non-UnrealMCP project C++ without the token | Existing C++ approval gate still applies. |
| Retry a mutation after an unknown outcome | Existing safety matrix routes to reconciliation rules; no automatic retry authorized. |

No safety-boundary weakening found in this bounded self-review. The changes clarify prose/routing rather than changing enforcement, executable workflows, or verification manifests; Tier 0 applies under cost-control.md. No independent reviewer was used.

## Measurements and validation

LF-normalized character counts for the six active files, excluding historical snapshots and this report:

| File | Before | After |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Root AGENTS.md | 4164 | 4520 |
| codex/AGENTS.md | 5949 | 6228 |
| Release SKILL.md | 3567 | 3110 |
| Release references | 1180 | 1394 |
| Safety SKILL.md | 2303 | 2415 |
| Safety references | 1050 | 1421 |

Total grows from 18213 to 19088 characters. This is a consistency improvement, not demonstrated context or latency savings; the diagnostic 35–50% reduction target was not met. Actual instruction loads, elapsed execution time, and token savings were not benchmarked.

- Both edited skills passed the bundled `quick_validate.py` using an isolated `uv run --no-project --with pyyaml` environment. Initial validation lacked PyYAML in the project environment; no project dependency change was required.
- Strict UTF-8 decoding, balanced Markdown fences, referenced Markdown path checks, and scoped `git diff --check` passed for active edits.
- Existing mixed line endings in one edited reference were normalized to CRLF; snapshots preserve original bytes, including mixed endings.
- Other dirty implementation/assets are outside this validation scope. No implementation full/build/live result is claimed.

## Review follow-up

The subsequent review found two omissions in the initial release-skill rewrite. Both were corrected before commit: `codex/docs/policies/git-repositories.md` now requires the complete intended staged diff to pass `git diff --cached --check` for every change type; the release skill explicitly includes executable workflow/configuration, shared-contract, and high-risk promotion and routes those cases to Tier 3 and release review. Tier 2 contract checks are also explicit. The skill format, UTF-8, fences, and scoped diff checks passed after correction. The six-file character counts above describe the initial candidate, not this follow-up; the final active scope includes the Git policy as a seventh file. Earlier self-review conclusions should be read with these two corrected findings.
